  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A thin convex lens is made of two materials with refractive indices <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></math> as shown in figure. The radius of curvature of the left and right spherical surfaces are equal. <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></math> is the focal length of the lens when <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The focal length is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></math> when <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Assuming <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo><</mo><mo><</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mn>1</mn><mo><</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo><</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo></math> the correct statement(s) is/are:<br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/pdherxyejecesdwwcdhehgshubvhoitzplkvkvkxvprxtqyjcw.png\"/></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "MLmMj",
      "text": "For  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>  and  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo></math>  the value of  <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>  will be  <math><mn>0.02</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>  (round off to  <math><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow></msup></math>  decimal place)",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "JQvVF",
      "text": "The relation between  <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>  and  <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>  remains unchanged if both the convex surfaces are replaced by concave surfaces of the same radius of curvature.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "lzdtJ",
      "text": "<math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&lt;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "GV9e2",
      "text": "If  <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>  then  <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
